WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.410
Natural law gives firm moral rules.

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:05.180
Do not kill the innocent.

3
00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:06.590
Do not lie.

4
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.240
Traditional Catholic teaching holds
some acts are intrinsically evil:

5
00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:14.580
wrong in themselves,
whatever the circumstances.

6
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.000
But hard cases press on this.

7
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.660
Picture a lie that would save a life.

8
00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:25.290
From the 1960s to the 1980s, Catholic
moral theologians argued over cases like

9
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:26.160
this.

10
00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:31.310
So can it be right to break a moral rule
without doing anything morally evil?

11
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.750
In this mission, you'll explore Bernard
Hoose's overview of that debate.

12
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:41.600
Then you'll weigh the case against it,
including a pope's rejection of it in 1993.

13
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:46.760
Your mission: find out whether breaking
a rule must always mean doing evil.
